sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor C1 as Client 1 (Leader)
    actor C2 as Client 2 (Follower)
    actor C50 as Clients 3..50 (Followers)
    participant I as EntityCacheInterceptor / AppCacheService
    participant Map as inFlightRequests (In-Memory Map)
    participant R as Redis (Testcontainers)
    participant DB as Database (PostgreSQL / ClickHouse)

    Note over C1,C50: 50 requests arrive within the same millisecond (Traffic Spike)

    par Parallel HTTP Requests
        C1->>I: GET /resource/123
        C2->>I: GET /resource/123
        C50->>I: GET /resource/123
    end

    Note over I,R: 1. Redis Lookup (Simultaneous Cache Miss)
    I->>R: GET cache:resource:123
    R-->>I: (null / undefined)

    Note over I,Map: 2. Concurrency Barrier (Request Coalescing)
    I->>Map: has("cache:resource:123")?
    Map-->>I: false (Client 1 wins race condition)
    
    I->>Map: set("cache:resource:123", leaderPromise)
    
    par Immediate Concurrency (Clients 2 to 50)
        C2->>I: has("cache:resource:123")? -> true
        I->>Map: get("cache:resource:123")
        Map-->>I: [In-Flight Promise]
        Note over C2,I: Client 2 awaits leader resolution
        C50->>I: has("cache:resource:123")? -> true
        I->>Map: get("cache:resource:123")
        Map-->>I: [In-Flight Promise]
        Note over C50,I: Clients 3..50 await leader resolution
    end

    Note over I,DB: 3. Single-Flight Execution: Only the Leader Hits the DB
    I->>DB: Execute expensive query (e.g., 150ms I/O latency)
    Note over DB: dbCallCount increments EXACTLY 1 time
    DB-->>I: Fresh payload computed

    Note over I,R: 4. Atomic Persistence with TTL
    I->>R: SET cache:resource:123, payload, PX: 10000
    R-->>I: OK

    Note over I,Map: 5. Cleanup In-Flight Map (finally block)
    I->>Map: delete("cache:resource:123")

    par Coalesced Broadcast to All Clients
        I-->>C1: 200 OK (Fresh Data)
        I-->>C2: 200 OK (Shared Data)
        I-->>C50: 200 OK (Shared Data)
    end